# AI Dashboard Assistant — host parity gate

When you add or materially change a **host dashboard write** (upload, send, status change, settings mutate, create/update entity) under org / property / parking:

## Same-change requirement

Choose **one** and document it in the PR / architecture catalog:

| Choice             | Do this                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            |
| ------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Assistant tool** | Add propose (+ execute if Tier 2) in `_shared/dashboardAssistant*.ts`, register in `TOOL_DECLARATIONS` + risk classifier + tool labels (edge + UI), update `docs/architecture/ai-dashboard-assistant.md` + manual test note. Prefer shared upload/service helpers — never a weaker chat-only path. |
| **Exclusion**      | Add a row under Explicit exclusions (or “Not built”) in `docs/architecture/ai-dashboard-assistant.md` with rationale, and a Host-facing knowledge Q&A (or KB sync) explaining how to finish in the UI.                                                                                             |

## Safety invariants (do not weaken)

1. Same backend + JWT RBAC as the dashboard endpoint.
2. Tier 0 / 1 / 2 + `external_send` as appropriate; Confirm freezes payload.
3. Chat attachments: path allowlist `{org}/{user}/{conversation}/…` only.
4. OTP-gated settings: require the same OTP / settings verification token — never bypass.
5. Never-build list stays catalog-enforced (irreversible destroyers, auto-reply send mode, etc.).

## Reads

New host-visible data surfaces should get a read tool **or** knowledge-base coverage so the assistant can answer without inventing facts.

